outcome:
The UI category guard (ui/src/test-categories.test.ts) rejects a `@vitest-environment` comment in a unit file, so one file can't take jsdom inside the node-environment unit project. But Vitest 4 picks a file's environment with /@(?:vitest|jest)-environment\s+([\w-]+)\b/ over the whole file text (getSpecificationsEnvironments in vitest's cli-api chunk). So a unit file with `@jest-environment jsdom` still gets jsdom, and nothing catches it.

Fix: use /@(?:vitest|jest)-environment\b/u, and mention both pragmas in docs/test.md and the guard comment.

Tidy-ups to fold in:
- rewrap the ~140-character line in docs/test.md near "The other three projects run in jsdom";
- tighten or drop the loose `toMatch(/environment,/u)` source check on vite.config.ts; the manifest check and the runtime typeof assertion already prove the environment;
- word the docs' "two cases" as examples ("such as"), since DOM access wrapped in try/catch is another case the node run doesn't fail.
